  "raw": {
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2174": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Data Science and Statistics",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Assistant Professor, Data Science and Statistics Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor, Data Science and Statistics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor, Data Science and Statistics Location Appleton Department Mathematics & Computer Science Position Type Faculty Position Description & Qualifications Lawrence University of Wisconsin, a selective undergraduate liberal arts college and conservatory of music located in Appleton, Wisconsin invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Data Science and Statistics to begin September 1, 2027. We seek candidates who will contribute to our growing program, which includes a new Data Science and Statistics major. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in statistics, biostatistics, data science, or a closely related field prior to the time of appointment (9/1/2027); ABD is acceptable for selection. Candidates should demonstrate potential for teaching a variety of undergraduate statistics and data science courses, and expect to participate in Lawrence’s flagship First Year Studies program on rotation. The First Year Studies curriculum presents an interdisciplinary introduction to the liberal arts intended to support new students’ fundamental skills as readers, writers, and thinkers. Primary duties include: teaching two undergraduate courses in each of Lawrence’s three ten-week terms, grading, advising and mentoring students; conducting research; leading occasional tutorials, supervising independent study projects and internships; assisting in curricular planning; and related departmental and institutional service. The successful candidate will be the third statistics and data science faculty member in the Department of Mathematics, Statistics, and Computer Science. Additional information about our curriculum and faculty can be found at https://www.lawrence.edu/academics/college/data-science-and-statistics . Candidates should submit the following: (1) a cover letter describing their interest in this position, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a statement of teaching explaining their pedagogical methods and teaching experiences, (4) a statement describing their scholarly activities, interests, and future plans, (5) names and email addresses for three references who can be contacted for letters of recommendation at a later stage in the process (at least one of whom can attest specifically to teaching). In their teaching statement, candidates are encouraged to discuss their experiences and ideas for teaching courses involving data analysis and computational tools. Candidates should also discuss how they will foster an inclusive and supportive learning environment for all students. In their scholarship statement, candidates are encouraged to discuss their experiences or ideas for incorporating undergraduate students in their research. Candidates are encouraged to read more about Lawrence at https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com as well as www.lawrence.edu and Colleges That Change Lives . We will begin reviewing applications on October 2, 2026. For further information, please contact Andrew Sage, the chair of the search committee ( sagea@lawrence.edu ). Posting Detail Information Posting Number S642P Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Graduate School Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Statement on Teaching List of References Statement on Scholarship Optional Documents Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2165": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Assistant Professor of Psychology Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Psychology Location Appleton Department Psychology Position Type Faculty Position Description & Qualifications Lawrence University of Wisconsin, a selective undergraduate liberal arts college and conservatory of music located in Appleton, Wisconsin, invites applications for two full-time tenure-track positions, at the rank of Assistant Professor of Psychology, to begin September 1, 2027. One position is in social psychology and the other position may be in one of the following areas: cognitive, biological, developmental or clinical/counseling psychology. We seek individuals who are dedicated teachers passionate about working with undergraduates in a liberal arts setting, active and engaging scholars, and effective mentors for students from diverse backgrounds. Successful candidates will teach Research Methods on rotation, as well as courses in their specialty area (at both the intermediate and advanced levels). One of these courses will involve a laboratory where students gain hands-on skills in research and/or applied psychology. Additionally, successful candidates will contribute to senior capstone and/or introductory psychology on rotation. Primary duties include: teaching, grading, advising and mentoring students; conducting research; leading occasional tutorials, supervising independent study projects and internships; assisting in curricular planning; and related departmental and institutional service. The teaching load is two courses per term (one course with 2 laboratory sections counts as a full load) for three ten-week terms a year, including participation in Lawrence’s flagship First Year Studies program on rotation. The First Year Studies curriculum presents an interdisciplinary introduction to the liberal arts intended to support new students’ fundamental skills as readers, writers, and thinkers. Candidates are expected to lead undergraduate research projects and connect scholarship with teaching. Laboratory space and start-up funds are available. Candidates must have a Ph.D. prior to the time of appointment (9/1/2027); ABD is acceptable for selection. For the social psychology position, the PhD must be in social psychology or closely related psychology subfield; for the second position, the Ph.D. must be in cognitive, biological, developmental, or clinical/counseling psychology or a closely related psychology subfield. Interested candidates should submit the following materials at: https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com : (1) a cover letter explaining your interest in Lawrence, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a teaching statement that includes your philosophy, teaching interests, information regarding how you will foster a truly engaged and supportive experience for undergraduates, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., syllabi, summary of teaching evaluations, etc.), (4) a research statement that includes a discussion of how you plan to engage undergraduates in research and how your research may be particularly suited to a liberal arts setting, and (5) a list of 3 references. Applications will be evaluated starting September 15, 2026. Candidates are encouraged to read about Lawrence and its surrounding community at Colleges That Change Lives, https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com, and www.lawrence.edu. For further information, please contact the Search Committee chair, Lori Hilt (lori.m.hilt@lawrence.edu). Posting Detail Information Posting Number S639P Number of Vacancies 2 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 32 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement on Teaching List of References Statement on Research Optional Documents Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
